---
import Guide from '../../layouts/Guide.astro';
import CenterCard from '../../components/CenterCard.astro';
import FloridaMap from '../../components/FloridaMap.astro';
import { centers, allColleges, stats } from '../../lib/centers';
import { SITE } from '../../lib/site';

const path = '/jewish-life-on-campus/florida/';
const colleges = allColleges();
const sorted = centers; // original site order
const ld = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'ItemList',
    name: 'Florida colleges and universities with Chabad on Campus',
    itemListElement: colleges.map((r, i) => ({ '@type': 'ListItem', position: i + 1, name: r.campus.name, url: `${SITE.url}${r.center.url}${r.campus.primary ? '' : '#' + r.campus.anchor}` })),
  },
];
---
<Guide
  title="Jewish life at Florida colleges"
  metaTitle="Jewish Life at Florida Colleges & Universities"
  description={`Jewish life at Florida colleges and universities: ${stats.campuses} schools welcomed by ${stats.centers} Chabad on Campus centers, from Tallahassee to Miami. Find yours.`}
  path={path}
  lead={`${stats.campuses} campuses. ${stats.centers} Chabad Houses. From Tallahassee to Miami.`}
  image="fl-florida"
  imageAlt="Students from Chabad at USF together with a USF flag"
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Jewish Life on Campus', href: '/jewish-life-on-campus/' }, { name: 'Florida', href: path }]}
  jsonLd={ld}
  wide
>
  <p>Florida is home to one of the largest Jewish communities in the country, and its campuses reflect that. Large public universities, small private colleges and community colleges all have a Chabad House nearby, and every one of them hosts Shabbat dinners, celebrates the Jewish holidays with students and is ready to welcome you.</p>

  <div class="mapwrap"><FloridaMap /></div>

  <h2>Chabad on Campus centers in Florida</h2>
  <p>Each center is led by a rabbi and rebbetzin who make their home your home. Some also welcome students from nearby colleges.</p>
  <div class="grid grid-3 cards">
    {sorted.map((c) => <CenterCard center={c} compact />)}
  </div>

  <h2>Every Florida college with Chabad on Campus</h2>
  <p>If your college is on this list, there is a Chabad House ready for you.</p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">College or university</th><th scope="col">Chabad center</th><th scope="col">City</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {colleges.map((r) => (
          <tr>
            <td><a href={r.campus.primary ? r.center.url : `${r.center.url}#${r.campus.anchor}`}>{r.campus.name}</a>{r.campus.abbr && <span class="muted"> ({r.campus.abbr})</span>}</td>
            <td><a href={r.center.url}>{r.center.officialName}</a></td>
            <td>{r.center.city}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Beyond your own campus</h2>
  <p>Florida's Chabad centers also bring students together across the state. Each year the <a href="/programs/florida-pegisha/">Florida Pegisha</a> gathers students from every Florida campus for one Shabbat weekend, and every student can join <a href="/programs/birthright-israel/">Birthright Israel with Chabad</a>, the <a href="/programs/pegisha/">International Pegisha</a> in New York and <a href="/programs/living-links/">Living Links</a>.</p>
</Guide>

<style>
  .mapwrap { max-width: 620px; margin: 48px 0 24px; }
  .cards { margin: 32px 0 16px; }
</style>
